.log files from package installs and reboot scheduling are also not confirmed removed, though the after-executor temporary-files inventory (which lists only systemd-private-* entries on both nodes) suggests /tmp was effectively reset by the reboots. All other state-changing commands (user/group creation, package install, directory/permission setup, exports config, service enable, mount setup, file writes, and the two node reboots) map directly to a material outcome or the required restart-evidence protocol. No destructive, broad, or security-weakening mutations were observed.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-cb645cb6eeb047d5\",\"global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files\",\"global:after_executor:node2:temporary-files\"]},\"overall_summary\":\"All material outcomes of the task are directly and consistently evidenced: the dataops identity (UID/GID 4500) exists on both nodes, /srv/nfs/shared is exported from node1 and mounted at /mnt/shared on node2, the directory carries dataops:dataops 2770 permissions on both sides, and bidirectional file creation under the shared identity preserves consistent ownership. The independent provider-wide restart protocol was also executed thoroughly for both nodes: pre-restart healthy baselines, reboot acknowledgements with observed unreachability, changed boot IDs cross-checked against the fixed lifecycle snapshots, and full recovery of the NFS service, export, mount, and prior data (plus a post-reboot write test) were all captured for both node1 and node2, including confirmation that node2's mount survived node1's restart without manual intervention.\",\"limitations\":[\"Cannot confirm whether the /tmp/dummy, /tmp/apt-nfs.log, or /tmp/reboot.log temp files were explicitly cleaned up versus implicitly cleared by the two reboots, since the after-executor temporary-files inventory may be bounded/filtered.\",\"No test was captured of a non-dataops user being denied access (mode 2770 group-restriction), though this was not explicitly required by the task.\"]}","structured_output":{"requirements":[{"id":"req-identity","requirement":"Create shared identity dataops with UID/GID 4500 on both node1 and node2","status":"satisfied","summary":"id dataops on both nodes shows uid=4500(dataops) gid=4500(dataops) groups=4500(dataops), created via matching groupadd/useradd commands.","evidence_ids":["cmd-faf6f8af52484504","cmd-c0b0d5a9447f444b"]},{"id":"req-export","requirement":"Export /srv/nfs/shared from node1 via NFS","status":"satisfied","summary":"/etc/exports populated with the share restricted to node2's IP, exportfs -ra applied, exportfs -v confirms active export, and nfs-kernel-server is active with ports 2049/111 listening.","evidence_ids":["cmd-ff18a9696a3a4192","cmd-0a9a896c041a4c8a"]},{"id":"req-mount","requirement":"Mount the export at /mnt/shared on node2","status":"satisfied","summary":"showmount confirms the export is visible from node2; mount -a mounts it as nfs4 at /mnt/shared with a persistent /etc/fstab entry added.","evidence_ids":["cmd-1f186c03f0ab46b8","cmd-5c60443101c242c3"]},{"id":"req-ownership-perms","requirement":"Shared directory owned dataops:dataops with mode 2770 on both sides","status":"satisfied","summary":"stat/ls output on node1 shows drwxrws--- dataops dataops (2770) for /srv/nfs/shared, and the same ownership/mode is visible through the mount on node2.","evidence_ids":["cmd-92377341af264763","cmd-c1cb2c4fb524499f"]},{"id":"req-bidirectional-consistency","requirement":"Files created on either system keep consistent ownership/permissions (bidirectional access via shared identity)","status":"satisfied","summary":"dataops user on node2 created from-node2.txt (dataops:dataops), visible from node1, which then created from-node1.txt (dataops:dataops), visible back on node2 with correct ownership on both sides.","evidence_ids":["cmd-38451ba1cbf44d2e","cmd-b08359d7a4234362","cmd-dda99705b4b34bbc"]}],"confidence":0.93,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.85,"summary":"One exploratory command 